msgctxt "oper.kind.ban.activate.label"
msgid "Bans activated"
msgstr "Активовані бани"

#. A nefarious2 server notice in plain words, shown in chat to an IRC operator (kind ban.activate). Each {placeholder} is filled from the notice and rendered as a nick, chip or plain text: keep every placeholder exactly, reorder freely, and do not inflect around them. Similar length to the English.
#. Placeholders: {oper} is the nick of the oper who did it; {server} is a server name; {type} is the ban type: G-line, K-line, Z-line, shun or 'channel ban' (translated separately); {mask} is a ban mask (a chip); {expires} is when it expires, already phrased ('in 3h', 'never'); {reason} is a reason, verbatim from the server or the oper. Only one of the two adjacent placeholders before the verb is ever filled (an oper's nick or a server name): keep them side by side.
#. {type} is the ban's kind as the server names it, in English (G-line, Z-line, Shun, K-line, Jupe); its grammatical gender in your language is unknown and varies, so write no article, adjective or verb ending that has to agree with it: use a neutral frame, e.g. 'ban ({type})' or '{type}:' — in English it reads 'a {type}'.
#: client/js/irc/profiles/noticeText.ts
msgctxt "oper.kind.ban.activate.template"
msgid "{oper}{server} activated the global {type} on {mask}, expiring {expires}: {reason}"
msgstr "{oper}{server}: активовано глобальний бан ({type}) на {mask} (спливає {expires}): {reason}"

